os1 was the manager, so after it stopped, port 9200 stayed silent, and both survivors named os3, the winner of a new election. The term went from 5 to 6: one election, one new term, the same bookkeeping as Raft's. The state's version went up by 3, because the new manager published several changes: os1 removed, a replica promoted, copies left without a node. When os1 came back, it rejoined as an ordinary member; managers don't hand the job back. Your node names, terms and versions will differ (each start of the cluster can take a few terms to settle), but the term always goes up by at least one.

